          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To set up Node.js in **Termux** within a **new directory**, follow these steps:\n\n### **Step 1: Install Termux & Update Packages**\n1. If you haven't already, install **Termux** from [F-Droid](https://f-droid.org/) or the Play Store.\n2. Open Termux and update your packages:  \n   ```sh\n   pkg update && pkg upgrade -y\n   ```\n\n### **Step 2: Install Node.js**\nNode.js is available in Termux. You can install it using:\n```sh\npkg install nodejs -y\n```\nAfter installation, check the version:\n```sh\nnode -v\nnpm -v  # To check if npm (Node Package Manager) is installed\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Create a New Directory & Navigate Into It**\nNow, create a new project directory where you want to set up Node.js:\n```sh\nmkdir my-node-project\ncd my-node-project\n```\n\n### **Step 4: Initialize a New Node.js Project**\nRun the following command to initialize a Node.js project"
          ]
        },
