        "create_time": 1739905843.135698,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Inside your new directory (`my-node-project`), initialize a new Node.js project by running:  \n\n```sh\nnpm init -y\n```\nThis will create a `package.json` file with default settings.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 5: Create a Simple Node.js Script**\nNow, create a basic Node.js script:  \n\n```sh\nnano index.js\n```\nInside `index.js`, add the following code:  \n\n```js\nconsole.log(\"Hello from Node.js in Termux!\");\n```\nSave and exit (`CTRL + X`, then `Y`, then `Enter`).\n\n---\n\n### **Step 6: Run the Node.js Script**\nExecute the script with:  \n\n```sh\nnode index.js\n```\nIf everything is set up correctly, you should see:  \n```\nHello from Node.js in Termux!\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Step 7: Install Additional Packages (Optional)**\nYou can install npm packages like Express:  \n\n```sh\nnpm install express\n```\n\nCheck installed packages with:  \n\n```sh\nnpm list --depth=0\n```\n\n---\n\nNow, your **Node.js environment** is successfully set up in **Termux**! Let me know if you need further help."
          ]
        },
