        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "The error **\"Cannot find module\"** in Termux usually happens due to:  \n\n1. A missing or incorrectly named JavaScript file.  \n2. Running the command from the wrong directory.  \n3. Issues with Node.js installation.  \n\n---\n\n### **Fix Steps:**\n\n#### **1. Check If `index.js` Exists**\nRun:\n```sh\nls -l\n```\n- If `index.js` is missing, recreate it:  \n  ```sh\n  nano index.js\n  ```\n  Add:\n  ```js\n  console.log(\"Hello from Node.js in Termux!\");\n  ```\n  Save with `CTRL + X`, then `Y`, then `Enter`.\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Run the Script with Full Path**\nIf your script is inside a different folder, specify the full path:\n```sh\nnode /data/data/com.termux/files/home/my-node-project/index.js\n```\nOr, navigate to the correct directory first:\n```sh\ncd ~/my-node-project\nnode index.js\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Check the Installed Node.js Version**\n```sh\nnode -v\n```\nIf Node.js is not installed, reinstall it:\n```sh\npkg install nodejs -y\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **4. Clear npm Cache (If Needed)**\n```sh\nnpm cache clean --force\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **5. Reinstall Node Modules (If Using npm Packages)**\n```sh\nrm -rf node_modules package-lock.json\nnpm install\n```\n\nTry these steps and let me know if the issue persists!"
          ]
        },
