          "parts": [
            "You can create a **Termux folder** in **Internal Storage** and set it up to work from there. Follow these steps carefully.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Grant Termux Storage Permission**\nFirst, you need to allow Termux to access Internal Storage:  \n```sh\ntermux-setup-storage\n```\n- A pop-up will ask for permission. **Allow it**.\n- This creates a `storage` directory in Termux.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Create a Folder in Internal Storage**\nNow, create a new folder inside Internal Storage. Run:\n```sh\nmkdir /data/data/com.termux/files/home/storage/shared/my-termux-project\n```\nAlternatively, you can create the folder manually using a file manager.\n\n---\n\n### **Step "
